{"ok":true,"data":{"kind":"tree","level":"L2","options":[{"name":"repo","valueName":"DIR","valueType":"path","defaultNote":"the nearest ancestor directory holding a canon.yaml","flagOnly":true,"help":"The repo to act on (default: the nearest ancestor directory holding a canon.yaml)"},{"name":"as","valueName":"ROLE","valueType":"enum","possibleValues":["planner","implementer","reviewer","orchestrator"],"env":"CANON_ROLE","flagOnly":true,"help":"The role you act as: planner, implementer, reviewer or orchestrator. Overrides `CANON_ROLE`. `schema` and `context` list only the role's commands, `status` keeps its steps, and `--role` on `evidence add` / `evidence audit` / `review scenario` / `review change` is this role unless given"},{"name":"limit","valueName":"N","valueType":"integer","default":100,"flagOnly":true,"domain":{"minimum":1},"help":"Return at most this many records per page"},{"name":"cursor","flagOnly":true,"help":"Resume after the last record of the previous page (the `nextCursor` it reported)"},{"name":"all","valueType":"switch","flagOnly":true,"help":"Return every record from the cursor on, not one page"},{"name":"dry-run","valueType":"switch","help":"Validate fully and report what would be written, without writing anything"},{"name":"manifest","valueName":"FILE","valueType":"path","required":true,"help":"Repository-relative input manifest"},{"name":"session","valueName":"SESSION_ID","domain":{"pattern":"^[^\\p{Cc}\\p{White_Space}]([^\\p{Cc}]*[^\\p{Cc}\\p{White_Space}])?$"},"help":"The acting session (recorded as actor.session_id); optional"},{"name":"project","valueName":"PROJECT_ID","domain":{"pattern":"^[a-z0-9]+(-[a-z0-9]+)*$"},"help":"Spec corpus id of the scenarios. Required only when canon.yaml configures more than one spec root"},{"name":"actor","valueName":"ACTOR_ID","required":true,"domain":{"pattern":"^\\p{White_Space}*([^\\p{Cc}\\p{Zl}\\p{Zp}]*[^\\p{Cc}\\p{White_Space}])\\p{White_Space}*$"},"help":"The reviewer recording this (recorded as the divergence's reviewer and actor)"},{"name":"approver","valueName":"NAME","domain":{"pattern":"^\\p{White_Space}*([^\\p{Cc}\\p{Zl}\\p{Zp}]*[^\\p{Cc}\\p{White_Space}])\\p{White_Space}*$"},"help":"With --relayed-via, who the human is"},{"name":"note","valueName":"TEXT","help":"With --relayed-via, the human's answer as they gave it"},{"name":"rev","default":"HEAD","help":"The commit this record is about: any git revision (`HEAD~1`, a branch, a tag, a short sha); the full sha is recorded with the code tree it saw. The default HEAD records the working tree as it stands (uncommitted code included), and a commit made from it has the same code tree. Outside git, or with no commit, the command refuses (COMMIT_REQUIRED)"},{"name":"round","valueName":"N","valueType":"integer","default":1,"domain":{"maximum":4294967295,"minimum":1},"help":"The review round this version belongs to (1-based)"},{"name":"detail","valueName":"TEXT","help":"Free-text detail recorded on the version (optional)"},{"name":"role","defaultNote":"the role declared with --as or CANON_ROLE","env":"CANON_ROLE","domain":{"pattern":"^[a-z0-9]+(-[a-z0-9]+)*$"},"help":"The role this record is attributed to (default: the role declared with --as / CANON_ROLE)"},{"name":"promote","valueType":"switch","defaultNote":"on under canon.yaml `write: { promote: auto }`","help":"Promote the record this run staged, in the same run; records others staged stay staged (the default under canon.yaml `write: { promote: auto }`)"},{"name":"no-promote","valueType":"switch","help":"Keep this write staged even under canon.yaml `write: { promote: auto }`"},{"name":"command-result","valueName":"TEXT","help":"The real captured output backing --summary (requires --summary; scanned for fabrication markers)"},{"name":"run","valueName":"RUN_ID","domain":{"pattern":"^[0-9A-HJKMNP-TV-Za-hjkmnp-tv-z]{26}$"},"help":"RunId (ULID) of the run that produced this evidence"},{"name":"report","valueName":"FORMAT:PATH","repeatable":true,"domain":{"pattern":"^(junit|cucumber|swift-testing):[^\u0000]+$"},"help":"EXPERIMENTAL: bind and parse a test report, `junit:<path>`, `cucumber:<path>` or `swift-testing:<path>`; repeatable"},{"name":"max-artifact-mib","valueName":"N","valueType":"integer","default":25,"domain":{"minimum":1},"help":"Per-file size limit for the artifact store (.canon/artifacts/sha256/), in MiB; a larger bound file is refused"},{"name":"override-reason","valueName":"TEXT","domain":{"pattern":"^\\p{White_Space}*([^\\p{Cc}\\p{Zl}\\p{Zp}]*[^\\p{Cc}\\p{White_Space}])\\p{White_Space}*$"},"help":"Attest anyway while a subject this record attests for has a brief awaiting the human's answer (one line of text, recorded on the record with --actor)"},{"name":"resolution-rev","valueName":"REV","defaultNote":"HEAD when --disposition is fixed","help":"The commit that closed it, any git revision (resolved to the full sha, with the code tree it saw). Permitted only with --disposition fixed, where it defaults to HEAD. Existence only; canon never reads the commit's message or diff"},{"name":"spec-root","valueName":"DIR","valueType":"path","help":"Sync exactly one ad hoc root, overriding canon.yaml's specs.roots[]"},{"name":"upstream-ref","valueName":"TEXT","help":"Provenance ref (mutually exclusive with --original-spec-ref; exactly one required)"},{"name":"original-spec-ref","valueName":"TEXT","help":"Provenance ref (mutually exclusive with --upstream-ref; exactly one required)"},{"name":"review-outcome","valueType":"enum","possibleValues":["signed","indeterminate","unavailable"],"default":"signed","help":"How the reviewer's run ended: signed (an approval), indeterminate (ran, reached no verdict) or unavailable (could not run). Only signed counts; the others are recorded as review gaps"},{"name":"reviewer-provider","valueName":"NAME","domain":{"pattern":"^[^\\p{Cc}\\p{White_Space}]([^\\p{Cc}]*[^\\p{Cc}\\p{White_Space}])?$"},"help":"The reviewer runtime's provider (e.g. anthropic, openai)"},{"name":"reviewer-model","valueName":"NAME","domain":{"pattern":"^[^\\p{Cc}\\p{White_Space}]([^\\p{Cc}]*[^\\p{Cc}\\p{White_Space}])?$"},"help":"The reviewer runtime's model id"},{"name":"reviewer-harness","valueName":"NAME","domain":{"pattern":"^[^\\p{Cc}\\p{White_Space}]([^\\p{Cc}]*[^\\p{Cc}\\p{White_Space}])?$"},"help":"The harness that ran the reviewer (e.g. omp, codex, claude)"},{"name":"artifact","valueName":"PATH","valueType":"path","repeatable":true,"help":"A file the reviewer looked at (screenshot, recording); repeatable; must be inside the repo. Stored in .canon/artifacts/sha256/ and re-hashed by `canon gate check`"},{"name":"skills-source","valueName":"DIR","valueType":"path","defaultNote":"CANON_SKILLS_SOURCE, else canon/skills","env":"CANON_SKILLS_SOURCE","help":"Source directory; defaults to CANON_SKILLS_SOURCE or canon/skills"},{"name":"harness","valueName":"NAME","valueType":"enum","possibleValues":["claude","codex","omp","pi"],"repeatable":true,"defaultNote":"the harnesses `skills install` would use","help":"A harness to inspect (repeatable, once per name): `claude`, `codex`, `omp` or `pi`. Omitted, and no `--no-harness`: as for install"},{"name":"no-harness","valueType":"switch","help":"Inspect no harness: the selection is an empty list"}],"commands":[{"command":"brief","kind":"group","summary":"Check a change's brief (PRD format) and see the next steps; never edits"},{"command":"brief check","summary":"Read the brief against the rules: blocker and advisory findings (exit 0 clean, 1 blockers, 2 refused)","effect":"read","x-canon":{"roles":["planner","reviewer"]}},{"command":"brief show","summary":"Show where the change stands and the next one to three steps; never edits","effect":"read","x-canon":{"roles":["planner","reviewer"]}},{"command":"completion","summary":"Write the shell completion script for canon (bash, zsh or fish)","effect":"read","x-canon":{"roles":"all"}},{"command":"context","summary":"Show what you can author here: record kinds, fields, enums, policies","effect":"read","x-canon":{"roles":"all"}},{"command":"divergence","kind":"group","summary":"Stage, promote, resolve, and inspect spec divergences"},{"command":"divergence add","summary":"Add a divergence candidate, staged with no run_seq yet (commit it with `canon gate promote --kind divergence`, or in the same run with --promote / `write: { promote: auto }`)","effect":"write","x-canon":{"roles":["implementer","reviewer"]}},{"command":"divergence defer","summary":"Directly record a deferred divergence (requires --reason/--expiry)","effect":"write","x-canon":{"roles":["implementer","reviewer"]}},{"command":"divergence list","summary":"List the current divergence burn-down state","effect":"read","x-canon":{"roles":"all"}},{"command":"divergence resolve","summary":"Directly record a resolved divergence","effect":"write","x-canon":{"roles":["implementer","reviewer"]}},{"command":"finding","kind":"group","summary":"Record one code-review finding as a durable record"},{"command":"finding add","summary":"Record one code-review finding (promoted in the same run under `write: { promote: auto }` or with --promote; under `write.promote: manual`, commit it with `canon gate promote`)","effect":"write","x-canon":{"roles":["reviewer"]}},{"command":"finding close","summary":"Move an already-committed finding's disposition (promoted in the same run under `write: { promote: auto }` or with --promote; under `write.promote: manual`, commit it with `canon gate promote`)","effect":"write","x-canon":{"roles":["reviewer"]}},{"command":"finding list","summary":"List a change's committed findings at their latest version: round, seq, severity, disposition, reviewer and summary","effect":"read","x-canon":{"roles":"all"}},{"command":"format","summary":"Validate a spec/artifact corpus against canon's format","effect":"read","x-canon":{"roles":"all"}},{"command":"gate","kind":"group","summary":"Run evidence gates, promote staged records, install hooks"},{"command":"gate check","summary":"Run the coverage/ledger/staleness/trust checks (0 clean, 1 red, 2 usage)","effect":"read","x-canon":{"roles":"all"}},{"command":"query","summary":"Read stored records across every storage tier","effect":"read","x-canon":{"roles":"all"}},{"command":"retrieve","summary":"Fetch role-scoped strategy guidance","effect":"read","x-canon":{"roles":"all"}},{"command":"review","kind":"group","summary":"Record an attributed review verdict"},{"command":"review change","summary":"Write one attributed Review record for a chore change directly to the ledger (exactly one provenance ref required). The review signs the chore's invariants and checks against the diff and pins the change's brief; an edit to the brief stales it. A chore needs exactly this one review before `subject move --to shipped`","effect":"write","x-canon":{"roles":["reviewer"]}},{"command":"review scenario","summary":"Write one attributed Review record per scenario directly to the ledger, nothing to promote (exactly one provenance ref required). A review pins the scenario's digest and what its latest evidence says (verdict and checks); it counts only while both are unchanged. Each scenario must be indexed, or nothing is written (exit 2)","effect":"write","x-canon":{"roles":["reviewer"]}},{"command":"schema","summary":"Describe canon's own commands: list them, or show one command's arguments, options, effect and exit codes","effect":"read","x-canon":{"roles":"all"}},{"command":"search","summary":"Search records, brief sections and scenario text, with each hit's neighbors in the record graph","effect":"read","x-canon":{"roles":"all"}},{"command":"skills","kind":"group","summary":"Install canon's agent guides into a repo"},{"command":"skills show","summary":"Print a guide built into this binary (markdown on stdout); the installed SKILL.md is a stub that points here","effect":"read","x-canon":{"roles":"all"}},{"command":"status","summary":"Show where this repo stands: subjects by status, their gaps, and the next commands","effect":"read","x-canon":{"roles":"all"}},{"command":"trace","summary":"Follow a finding's review loop in time order: review, finding, fix, re-review, evidence","effect":"read","x-canon":{"roles":"all"}}],"x-canon":{"as":"reviewer","rolesForm":"x-canon.roles of a command is the string all (every role) or an array of role names; an empty array is humans only"}},"meta":{"command":"schema","schemaVersion":"1.6","tool":"canon","toolVersion":"0.41.0","contract":"atip/1","contractVersion":"1.6"}}
